{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019H7EotbQSAVVqjFhvP67fB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed imagined/predicted experimental results for all planned experiments in the experiment plan, under the \"best\" tier scenario. Each prediction needs a result_rationale explaining why this outcome would occur under the best tier.\n\nLet me carefully go through each planned experiment and generate realistic predicted results that are consistent with the best tier definition and the key metric ranges provided.\n\nLet me organize by experiment:\n\n1. **exp-001**: Task-specificity characterization - already has some results, need to flesh out\n\n\n2. **exp-002**: Multi-benchmark per-example analysis\n3. **exp-003**: Helped/hurt sample characterization\n4. **exp-004**: Attention weight extraction\n5. **exp-005**: Architecture expansion check\n6. **exp-006**: CANCELLED\n7. **exp-007**: 340M rebound mechanism\n8. **exp-008**: Statistical robustness framework\n9. **exp-009**: Wang et al. differentiation\n10. **exp-010**: Convergence-divergence bridge\n\nNow I need to work through each of these experiments and generate predicted results that align with the best tier metrics: lambada_std_reduction_bootstrap_ci_pct in the [70, 88] range, lambada_rho_bootstrap_ci between [-1.0, -0.85], and the arc metrics.\n\nFor the best tier, I'm looking at strong negative correlations on ARC/HellaSwag (rho around -0.9 to -0.7), with only 2-3 benchmarks showing rho below -0.5, and Jaccard similarity staying low around 0.03-0.09. The sample-level features are highly significant (p-values down to 1e-06), attention correlations are moderate to strong (0.4-0.7), and we're testing 4-5 different architectures. The core finding is that per-example analysis reveals task-specific non-convergence patterns, with at least 3 features significantly distinguishing helped versus hurt samples even after excluding the GDN.\n\nThe key validations across experiments show that attention patterns correlate meaningfully with per-example effects, the 95% confidence intervals hold up under bootstrap resampling, and the main claims survive both GDN exclusion and multiple comparison correction. I'm also checking whether this pattern replicates across additional architectures like Mamba hybrids, and whether the 340M model's rebound has a clear mechanistic explanation tied to capacity constraints that aligns with the 1.3B behavior. The ARC-Easy correlation should strengthen further once I apply the per-example lens.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10641,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10641},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc1945c5-caea-4246-8ef4-0ee4426cff4c","uuid":"e66f26f8-f92c-4871-b54b-40926d42968e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019H7EotbQSAVVqjFhvP67fB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  所有实验均确认或加强现有发现。Continuous retrieval-demand spectrum 成立且有 ≥2 个锚点\n  （LAMBADA ρ=-1.0, ARC-Easy ρ≈-0.85）。Mechanistic evidence 完整：sample feature\n  区分 + attention pattern 相关性形成因果链。额外架构（Mamba hybrid）复现收敛模式。\n  340M rebound 有 capacity bottleneck 解释，与 1.3B 形成连贯叙事。GDN 排除后三条 claim\n  均成立。直投 EMNLP Main，title 用 \"The Equalizer Paradox\"。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Task-specificity characterization of equalizer effect\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      对 6 个 benchmark 计算 1.3B 下各 attention ratio 的 cross-architecture std，\n      建立 convergence strength（Spearman ρ）与 retrieval demand 的连续关系。\n    expected_results:\n      lambada_rho: -1.0\n      lambada_std_reduction_pct: 79\n      arc_easy_rho: -0.7\n      arc_challenge_rho: -0.3\n      hellaswag_rho: -0.1\n      winogrande_rho: 0.05\n      mmlu_rho: 0.1\n      benchmarks_with_rho_below_neg05: 2\n    result_rationale: >\n      LAMBADA 是纯 last-word retrieval 任务，attention 的 key-value lookup 机制天然对齐\n      这类需求，因此跨架构方差压缩最彻底（ρ=-1.0）。ARC-Easy 含大量事实检索型题目，\n      attention 部分有效（ρ=-0.7）。HellaSwag/WinoGrande/MMLU 以推理、常识、世界知识为主，\n      attention 的收敛作用被 recurrence core 的架构差异主导，ρ 趋近零。这形成了以 retrieval\n      demand 为横轴的 dose-response 曲线，两个显著锚点（LAMBADA + ARC-Easy）足以建立\n      continuous spectrum 的可信度。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Cross-architecture convergence by benchmark\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Retrieval Demand (BIG-bench)\", \"ρ (std vs attn ratio)\", \"p-value (permutation)\", \"Std at ratio=0\", \"Std at ratio=24\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LAMBADA\", \"High\", \"-1.00\", \"0.0083\", \"0.024\", \"0.005\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Easy\", \"Medium-High\", \"-0.70\", \"0.117\", \"0.031\", \"0.018\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Challenge\", \"Medium\", \"-0.30\", \"0.347\", \"0.022\", \"0.019\"]\n          - [\"HellaSwag\", \"Low\", \"-0.10\", \"0.782\", \"0.018\", \"0.017\"]\n          - [\"WinoGrande\", \"Low-Medium\", \"0.05\", \"0.912\", \"0.015\", \"0.016\"]\n          - [\"MMLU\", \"Low\", \"0.10\", \"0.782\", \"0.028\", \"0.027\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 1a: 散点图，x=retrieval demand（连续量化），y=Spearman ρ，6 个 benchmark 标注。拟合线 R²≈0.85，显示 dose-response 关系。\"\n      - \"Fig 1b: 折线图，x=attention ratio (0,1,3,6,8,24)，y=cross-arch std，每条线一个 benchmark。LAMBADA 单调下降，ARC-Easy 下降但较平缓，其余平坦。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Continuous retrieval-demand spectrum 成立。避免了 binary retrieval/reasoning 分类的\n      post-hoc cherry-picking 风险。BIG-bench taxonomy 提供外部锚定。LAMBADA + ARC-Easy\n      两个锚点形成梯度，其余 benchmark 填充低端。Reviewer Concern B 通过 dose-response\n      framing 化解。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark per-example analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      对 1.3B 模型（GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 × 5 attention ratios）和 10×340M 模型重新运行\n      lm-eval --log_samples，收集 HellaSwag、ARC-Easy、ARC-Challenge 的 per-example 数据。\n      分析 per-example 层面是否存在 convergence 或 task-specific divergence。\n    expected_results:\n      hellaswag_per_example_convergence: false\n      hellaswag_per_example_pattern: \"systematic architecture-specific, not random noise\"\n      arc_easy_per_example_convergence: true\n      arc_easy_rho_after_per_example: -0.85\n      arc_easy_jaccard_pairwise: 0.12\n      arc_challenge_per_example_convergence: false\n      arc_challenge_per_example_pattern: \"weak, architecture-independent noise\"\n      models_evaluated: 23\n      gpu_hours_actual: 18\n    result_rationale: >\n      HellaSwag 在 aggregate 层面无收敛（ρ=-0.1），per-example 分析确认这不是 power 问题而是\n      真阴性——attention 在不同架构上改变不同 sample 的正确率，但这些变化是 systematic\n      architecture-specific（每个架构有自己稳定的 helped/hurt subset），而非 random noise。\n      这说明 attention 在推理任务上\"做了事\"但没有跨架构趋同。ARC-Easy 在 per-example 层面\n      发现 attention 确实压缩了跨架构差异：对 retrieval-heavy 子题（事实召回型），三个架构的\n      正确率 variance 下降；对 reasoning-heavy 子题则无变化。这将 aggregate ρ 从 -0.70\n      加强至 -0.85（通过去除 reasoning 子题噪声）。ARC-Easy 成为 continuous spectrum 的\n      第二个强锚点。ARC-Challenge 因推理占比高，per-example 无系统模式。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Per-example convergence metrics by benchmark\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"N samples\", \"Aggregate ρ\", \"Per-example ρ (filtered)\", \"Jaccard (pairwise mean)\", \"Pattern type\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LAMBADA\", \"5153\", \"-1.00\", \"-1.00\", \"0.06\", \"Architecture-specific convergence\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Easy\", \"2376\", \"-0.70\", \"-0.85\", \"0.12\", \"Retrieval-subset convergence\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Challenge\", \"1172\", \"-0.30\", \"-0.25\", \"0.31\", \"No systematic pattern\"]\n          - [\"HellaSwag\", \"10042\", \"-0.10\", \"-0.08\", \"0.22\", \"Systematic but non-converging\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 2a: Heatmap，rows=HellaSwag samples (clustered)，cols=models (sorted by arch×attn ratio)。显示 per-example correctness pattern 是 architecture-clustered 而非 attention-ratio-clustered，确认非收敛。\"\n      - \"Fig 2b: ARC-Easy 子集分析——retrieval-type vs reasoning-type 题目分别画 cross-arch std 曲线。Retrieval 子集下降明显（ρ=-0.85），reasoning 子集平坦。\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-002 的 best 结果是双重确认：(1) HellaSwag/ARC-C 在 per-example 层面确认非收敛，\n      升级 task-specificity 从\"aggregate insignificant\"到\"per-example confirmed non-converging\"；\n      (2) ARC-Easy 在去噪后 ρ 加强至 -0.85，成为第二个强锚点。Continuous spectrum 从\n      单点（LAMBADA）变为双锚点梯度，极大加强 Claim 1。\n\n  - name: \"Helped/hurt sample characterization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对 LAMBADA 上各架构的 helped/hurt samples 计算 token frequency、context length、\n      last-sentence perplexity、domain 分布。测试 feature 是否区分 helped/hurt，且跨架构\n      feature profile 是否不同。\n    expected_results:\n      n_features_significant_p001: 3\n      best_feature: \"target_token_frequency\"\n      best_feature_p: 2.5e-05\n      second_feature: \"context_length\"\n      second_feature_p: 3.1e-04\n      third_feature: \"last_sentence_perplexity\"\n      third_feature_p: 8.7e-04\n      gdn_profile: \"helped on rare tokens + long contexts\"\n      retnet_profile: \"helped on high-perplexity last sentences\"\n      hgrn2_profile: \"helped broadly but strongest on medium-frequency tokens\"\n      cross_arch_profile_difference_p: 0.0003\n      effect_size_cohens_d_best: 0.72\n    result_rationale: >\n      GatedDeltaNet 的 delta rule 机制擅长 associative recall，attention 补充的是对\n      rare token 的 precise retrieval（delta rule 对 rare token 的 update 不够精确），\n      因此 GDN helped samples 集中在 rare token + long context（需要远距离检索）。RetNet\n      的 exponential decay 使其对 last sentence 内的局部信息较强，attention 补充的是\n      high-perplexity last sentence 中的 disambiguation（decay 无法区分多个候选），因此\n      RetNet helped samples 集中在 high-perplexity last sentence。HGRN2 的 hierarchical\n      gating 提供多尺度记忆但对 token frequency 有 sweet spot，attention 拓宽了这个\n      sweet spot。三种架构的 feature profile 统计显著不同（p<0.001），这直接解释了为什么\n      Jaccard overlap 低——它们被 attention 帮助的 sample 具有不同的语言学特征。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Feature importance for helped/hurt classification by architecture\"\n        columns: [\"Feature\", \"GDN (AUC)\", \"RetNet (AUC)\", \"HGRN2 (AUC)\", \"Overall p-value\", \"Cross-arch difference p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Target token freq (log rank)\", \"0.71\", \"0.58\", \"0.64\", \"2.5e-05\", \"0.0012\"]\n          - [\"Context length (tokens)\", \"0.67\", \"0.55\", \"0.57\", \"3.1e-04\", \"0.0089\"]\n          - [\"Last-sentence perplexity\", \"0.56\", \"0.69\", \"0.61\", \"8.7e-04\", \"0.0003\"]\n          - [\"Domain (topic entropy)\", \"0.54\", \"0.53\", \"0.55\", \"0.042\", \"0.31\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 3a: 三列 violin plot，每列一个架构，y=target token frequency，分 helped/hurt。GDN 的 helped 明显偏 rare（高 rank），RetNet 和 HGRN2 差异较小。\"\n      - \"Fig 3b: Radar chart，三个架构各一条线，四个 feature 为轴。显示 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 各有不同的 feature profile 'shape'，视觉化 mechanism specificity。\"\n      - \"Fig 3c: 2D embedding (UMAP on feature space)，helped samples 用架构颜色标注。三个架构的 helped clusters 空间分离。\"\n    analysis: >\n      3 个 feature 在 p<0.001 水平显著区分 helped/hurt，且跨架构 profile 统计显著不同。\n      这为 Claim 3（architecture-specific mechanism）提供了 feature-level 解释：不是抽象的\n      \"不同 sample\"，而是\"不同语言学特征的 sample\"。Feature profile 差异直接映射到各架构\n      recurrence core 的已知机制特性（delta rule → rare token recall; exponential decay\n      → local disambiguation; hierarchical gating → multi-scale memory）。\n\n  - name: \"Attention weight extraction and visualization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      从 h3-1 配置的三个架构提取 attention weight，分析 attention pattern 与 per-example\n      helped/hurt identity 的相关性，以及跨架构 attention pattern 的相似度。\n    expected_results:\n      attention_per_example_correlation_gdn: 0.52\n      attention_per_example_correlation_retnet: 0.61\n      attention_per_example_correlation_hgrn2: 0.48\n      attention_per_example_correlation_mean: 0.54\n      cross_arch_attention_similarity: 0.23\n      gdn_attention_focus: \"distributed over long-range context tokens\"\n      retnet_attention_focus: \"concentrated on last-sentence tokens\"\n      hgrn2_attention_focus: \"hierarchical — split between local and mid-range\"\n      gpu_hours_actual: 3.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      Attention layer 在不同 recurrence backbone 上学到了不同的 attention pattern，因为\n      它在补偿各架构 recurrence core 的不同弱点。GDN 的 delta rule 已经做了一定的\n      associative memory，attention 学会关注 long-range context（补充 delta rule 的\n      远距离衰减）。RetNet 的 exponential decay 快速遗忘远距离信息，attention 集中在\n      last-sentence 内做 disambiguation（因为 RetNet 对近距离信息已经较强）。HGRN2 的\n      hierarchical gating 在多个尺度上保留信息但每个尺度都不够精确，attention 学会\n      hierarchical 分配。这些不同的 attention pattern 与 helped/hurt sample 的对应关系\n      ≥0.4（最高 RetNet 0.61），因为 attention 的\"关注什么\"直接决定了\"帮助哪些 sample\"。\n      跨架构 attention similarity 仅 0.23，远低于随机基线 0.5，这是 mechanistic evidence\n      的核心：同样的 attention 架构在不同 recurrence backbone 上学到了完全不同的行为。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Attention pattern analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Attention focus\", \"Corr with helped/hurt\", \"p-value\", \"Mean entropy\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GDN\", \"Long-range distributed\", \"0.52\", \"1.2e-04\", \"3.41\"]\n          - [\"RetNet\", \"Last-sentence concentrated\", \"0.61\", \"8.7e-06\", \"2.18\"]\n          - [\"HGRN2\", \"Hierarchical split\", \"0.48\", \"4.3e-04\", \"2.89\"]\n      - name: \"Table 4b: Cross-architecture attention similarity (cosine)\"\n        columns: [\"Pair\", \"Mean cosine sim\", \"Significance vs random baseline\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GDN-RetNet\", \"0.19\", \"p<0.001 (below random)\"]\n          - [\"GDN-HGRN2\", \"0.27\", \"p=0.003 (below random)\"]\n          - [\"RetNet-HGRN2\", \"0.24\", \"p=0.001 (below random)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 4a: 三个 attention heatmap（每架构一个），同一组 LAMBADA sample，sorted by helped/hurt。可视化 attention 在 helped sample 上的 pattern 差异。\"\n      - \"Fig 4b: Attention entropy distribution per architecture。RetNet 的 attention 最集中（低 entropy），GDN 最分散。\"\n      - \"Fig 4c: 因果链图示：recurrence mechanism → attention adaptation → sample-specific effect → aggregate convergence。用箭头和数值标注每步的 correlation。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Mean correlation 0.54（range 0.48–0.61）超过 pass_fail 阈值 0.4，提供了 mechanistic\n      evidence 的第二根支柱。与 exp-003 的 feature 分析合在一起，形成完整因果链：\n      recurrence core 特性 → attention 学到补偿性 pattern → 补偿作用在不同语言学特征\n      的 sample 上生效 → 各架构 aggregate 性能趋同但 per-example 效果不重叠。\n      这回应 Reviewer Concern C（\"no causal mechanism\"），从 correlation 升级到\n      directed mechanistic narrative。\n\n  - name: \"Architecture expansion check\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      搜索 Wang et al. model zoo 及其他来源，找到额外的 hybrid 架构（Mamba hybrid 等），\n      在 LAMBADA 上评估收敛模式是否复现。\n    expected_results:\n      additional_architectures_found: 1\n      architecture_name: \"Mamba2-Attn hybrid (from community reproduction)\"\n      architecture_type: \"selective state space + attention\"\n      lambada_convergence_confirmed: true\n      mamba2_rho: -0.90\n      mamba2_std_reduction_pct: 71\n      mamba2_jaccard_with_others: 0.05\n      total_architectures_tested: 4\n      gpu_hours_actual: 5\n    result_rationale: >\n      Mamba2 的 selective state space mechanism 与 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 的 linear recurrence\n      不同（selection mechanism vs gating/delta rule/exponential decay），但 attention\n      的补偿效应仍然成立：Mamba2 的 state selection 对某类 retrieval pattern 较弱，\n      attention 补充后 aggregate 性能趋同。ρ=-0.90（略弱于 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 的 -1.0）\n      可能因为 Mamba2 hybrid 的 attention 集成方式略有不同（interleaved vs stacked），\n      但趋势一致。Jaccard 0.05 表明 Mamba2 的 helped/hurt subset 与其他三个架构同样\n      不重叠，进一步支持 architecture-specific mechanism。n=4 架构使得 Reviewer Concern D\n      （\"n=3 too few\"）大幅缓解。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Architecture expansion — convergence on LAMBADA\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Recurrence type\", \"ρ (std vs attn ratio)\", \"Std reduction %\", \"Jaccard with GDN\", \"Jaccard with RetNet\", \"Jaccard with HGRN2\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GDN\", \"Gated delta rule\", \"-1.00\", \"79%\", \"—\", \"0.06\", \"0.04\"]\n          - [\"RetNet\", \"Linear attn + exp decay\", \"-1.00\", \"79%\", \"0.06\", \"—\", \"0.08\"]\n          - [\"HGRN2\", \"Hierarchical gating\", \"-1.00\", \"79%\", \"0.04\", \"0.08\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Mamba2-Attn\", \"Selective state space\", \"-0.90\", \"71%\", \"0.05\", \"0.04\", \"0.07\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 5: 四条 convergence 曲线（cross-arch std vs attention ratio），LAMBADA。原三架构 + Mamba2-Attn。Mamba2 曲线形状一致但略高，汇入同一趋势。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Mamba2-Attn 的加入将 architectures_tested 从 3 提升到 4，覆盖了四种不同的 recurrence\n      mechanism。收敛模式复现（ρ=-0.90, std reduction 71%），且 Jaccard 保持低水平，\n      说明 equalizer effect 不是三个特定架构的巧合，而是 attention + any recurrence 的\n      通用现象。这是 generalization evidence 的最佳结果，直接提升论文的 impact 和\n      reviewer 的信任度。\n\n  - name: \"340M rebound mechanism analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      深入分析 340M 在 attn=8 时的非单调 rebound。与 1.3B 同 attention ratio 做\n      per-example 对比，识别 diverge 的 sample 并 characterize rebound 机制。\n    expected_results:\n      rebound_mechanism: \"capacity bottleneck\"\n      rebound_explanation: >\n        340M 在 attn ratio=8 时，attention 参数占总参数比例过高（~30%），\n        压缩了 recurrence core 的有效容量。Recurrence core 性能下降的 sample\n        与 attention 新帮助的 sample 不完全重叠，导致 aggregate std 回升。\n      rebound_samples_n: 412\n      rebound_samples_overlap_with_1_3b_hurt: 0.73\n      capacity_ratio_at_rebound: 0.31\n      capacity_ratio_at_monotonic_1_3b: 0.12\n      scale_contrast_narrative: >\n        1.3B 有足够容量同时支持 recurrence core 和 attention，两者互补；\n        340M 在高 attention ratio 时两者竞争参数预算，形成 capacity bottleneck。\n      training_tokens_confound_ruled_out: true\n      confound_evidence: \"per-example rebound pattern matches capacity prediction, not token-count prediction\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      340M 模型总参数有限，attention layer 的参数开销在 ratio=8 时占比达到 ~31%，\n      远高于 1.3B 同 ratio 时的 ~12%。这种参数预算竞争导致 recurrence core 的\n      effective capacity 下降。具体表现为：340M 在 ratio=8 时有 412 个 sample\n      从 correct 变为 incorrect（这些 sample 在 ratio=6 时还是 correct），其中 73%\n      在 1.3B ratio=8 时仍然 correct——说明问题在于 capacity 而非 attention 本身的\n      负面效应。训练 token 数量差异（20B vs 100B）作为 confound 被排除：如果是 token\n      count 导致，则 rebound 应该在所有 sample 上均匀分布；但实际 rebound 集中在\n      需要 strong recurrence（长距离依赖 + 高 token frequency）的 sample 上，\n      符合 capacity bottleneck 预测而非 token-count 预测。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: 340M rebound characterization\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"340M ratio=6\", \"340M ratio=8 (rebound)\", \"1.3B ratio=8\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Cross-arch std\", \"0.009\", \"0.014\", \"0.006\", \"340M rebounds, 1.3B continues declining\"]\n          - [\"Attention param ratio\", \"0.23\", \"0.31\", \"0.12\", \"340M capacity squeeze at ratio=8\"]\n          - [\"Rebound samples (became incorrect)\", \"—\", \"412\", \"0 (still correct)\", \"Capacity bottleneck\"]\n          - [\"Rebound sample features\", \"—\", \"Long context + high-freq tokens\", \"N/A\", \"Needs strong recurrence\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 6a: Dual y-axis plot，x=attention ratio。Left y=cross-arch std（340M 和 1.3B 两条线）。Right y=attention param ratio。340M 在 param ratio>0.3 处 rebound，1.3B 在 param ratio<0.15 范围内持续下降。\"\n      - \"Fig 6b: Venn diagram，340M rebound samples vs 1.3B hurt samples。73% overlap 标注。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Capacity bottleneck 机制清晰且有 falsifiable prediction（如果是 capacity 问题，\n      则 rebound samples 应集中在 recurrence-demanding 特征上——已验证）。排除了\n      training token confound。340M vs 1.3B 的对比从 aggregate 观察（\"scale matters\"）\n      升级为 mechanistic explanation（\"sufficient capacity is prerequisite for attention\n      to complement rather than compete with recurrence\"）。这为 Claim 2 提供了\n      two-scale 情况下能达到的最强叙事。\n\n  - name: \"Statistical robustness framework\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      Bootstrap CI、多重比较校正、GDN 排除敏感性分析、effect size 报告。\n    expected_results:\n      lambada_std_reduction_bootstrap_ci_pct: [72, 86]\n      lambada_std_reduction_point: 79\n      lambada_rho_bootstrap_ci: [-1.0, -0.90]\n      lambada_rho_point: -1.0\n      bonferroni_corrected_lambada_p: 0.050\n      fdr_corrected_lambada_p: 0.025\n      lambada_survives_correction: true\n      arc_easy_survives_correction: false\n      gdn_excluded_lambada_rho: -1.0\n      gdn_excluded_std_reduction: 74\n      gdn_excluded_claim1_survives: true\n      gdn_excluded_claim2_survives: true\n      gdn_excluded_claim3_survives: true\n      claims_surviving_gdn_exclusion: 3\n      cohens_d_lambada_convergence: 1.84\n      eta_squared_attention_ratio_effect: 0.67\n      bootstrap_iterations: 10000\n    result_rationale: >\n      LAMBADA 的 convergence effect size 极大（Cohen's d=1.84），Bootstrap 10000 次\n      迭代后 CI [72%, 86%] 不跨零，即使取下界 72% 仍是强效应。Bonferroni 校正\n      （6 benchmarks → α=0.0083）后 LAMBADA 仍显著（原始 p=0.0083，校正后刚好\n      在边界但通过），FDR 校正更宽松（p=0.025）。ARC-Easy 因 power 不足在 Bonferroni\n      后不显著（p=0.117），但在 continuous spectrum 叙事中作为\"suggestive\"仍有价值。\n      GDN 排除后（n=2 架构 + Mamba2），LAMBADA ρ 保持 -1.0（RetNet 和 HGRN2 本身就\n      呈现完美单调收敛），std reduction 从 79% 降至 74%（因样本量减少，估计略保守），\n      但三条 claim 均成立。这是因为 GDN 虽有 D004 confound，但 convergence 不依赖 GDN——\n      任意两个架构之间都呈现收敛。Claim 3 在 GDN 排除后也成立因为 RetNet vs HGRN2 的\n      Jaccard 仅 0.08，且 effect direction 相反（RetNet hurt, HGRN2 helped）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Bootstrap confidence intervals\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Point estimate\", \"Bootstrap 95% CI\", \"Survives Bonferroni?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LAMBADA std reduction %\", \"79%\", \"[72%, 86%]\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"LAMBADA ρ\", \"-1.00\", \"[-1.00, -0.90]\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Easy ρ\", \"-0.85\", \"[-1.00, -0.50]\", \"No (suggestive)\"]\n          - [\"Cross-arch Jaccard mean\", \"0.06\", \"[0.03, 0.09]\", \"N/A\"]\n      - name: \"Table 7b: GDN exclusion sensitivity\"\n        columns: [\"Claim\", \"With GDN\", \"Without GDN\", \"Survives?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Claim 1 (task-specific convergence)\", \"ρ=-1.0, 79% reduction\", \"ρ=-1.0, 74% reduction\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"Claim 2 (scale-dependent)\", \"340M partial, 1.3B complete\", \"Same pattern (RetNet/HGRN2/Mamba2)\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"Claim 3 (arch-specific mechanism)\", \"Jaccard=0.06, 3 profiles\", \"Jaccard=0.08, 2+1 profiles\", \"Yes\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 7: Bootstrap distribution plots。Left: std reduction %（vertical line at 0，distribution 远在右侧）。Right: ρ（distribution 远在 -1 附近）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      统计框架完整且所有核心 claim 通过 robustness check。GDN exclusion 是最关键的\n      sensitivity test（因为 GDN 有 D004 confound），三条 claim 均成立。LAMBADA 在\n      多重比较后仍显著是 best tier 的关键指标——Bonferroni 边界通过（p=0.0083 for\n      6 tests, observed p=0.0083）。Bootstrap CI 范围 [72%, 86%] 完全落在 best tier\n      指标范围 [70, 88] 内。\n\n  - name: \"Wang et al. explicit differentiation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      逐点对比 Wang et al. 的 exact statements 与我们的分析，建立清晰的四点增量。\n    expected_results:\n      wang_convergence_mentions: 3\n      wang_quantitative_convergence: 0\n      wang_per_example_analysis: 0\n      wang_scale_dependent_analysis: 0\n      wang_mechanistic_analysis: 0\n      differentiation_points: 4\n      wang_exact_quotes_extracted: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      Wang et al. 的论文是 model zoo paper，核心贡献是训练并开源 72 个模型。他们对\n      convergence 的提及限于 qualitative observations（如 \"performance gap narrows\n      with more attention layers\"），没有 (a) 计算 cross-arch std trajectories 或\n      Spearman ρ，(b) 做 per-example analysis，(c) 分析 scale dependency of convergence，\n      (d) 提供 mechanistic explanation。我们的增量恰好是他们没做的四件事。这四点\n      differentiation 在 paper 中以 explicit side-by-side table 呈现，让 reviewer\n      一目了然。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Systematic comparison with Wang et al. (2025)\"\n        columns: [\"Analysis dimension\", \"Wang et al.\", \"This work\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Cross-arch convergence quantification\", \"Qualitative ('gap narrows')\", \"Spearman ρ=-1.0, std reduction 79%, bootstrap CI\"]\n          - [\"Per-example mechanism\", \"Not analyzed\", \"Jaccard<0.10, architecture-specific helped/hurt subsets\"]\n          - [\"Scale dependency\", \"Not analyzed\", \"Binary contrast: 340M partial (rebound) vs 1.3B complete, capacity bottleneck mechanism\"]\n          - [\"Task-specificity\", \"Not analyzed\", \"Continuous retrieval-demand spectrum, 6 benchmarks, dose-response curve\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 8: Side-by-side visualization。Left: Wang et al. 的 aggregate performance table（screenshot with citation）。Right: 我们的 convergence curve + per-example heatmap，annotated with the four increments。\"\n    analysis: >\n      四点 differentiation 清晰且无重叠。我们使用 Wang et al. 的 model zoo（proper\n      attribution）但提供了他们完全没有的分析维度。这回应 Reviewer Risk 4 和 Concern E，\n      将我们的贡献从\"also studied convergence\"提升到\"discovered and characterized a\n      phenomenon they only glimpsed qualitatively\"。\n\n  - name: \"Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      在 LAMBADA 上，以 attention ratio 为 x 轴，同时绘制 aggregate convergence（cross-arch std）\n      和 per-example divergence（Jaccard, net effect asymmetry），展示 paradox 的共同演化。\n    expected_results:\n      convergence_divergence_correlation: -0.94\n      convergence_divergence_p: 0.005\n      paradox_strengthens_with_attention: true\n      jaccard_at_ratio_0: \"N/A (no attention effect)\"\n      jaccard_at_ratio_1: 0.08\n      jaccard_at_ratio_6: 0.06\n      jaccard_at_ratio_24: 0.04\n      std_at_ratio_0: 0.024\n      std_at_ratio_24: 0.005\n      net_effect_asymmetry_gdn: -0.12\n      net_effect_asymmetry_retnet: -0.08\n      net_effect_asymmetry_hgrn2: 0.11\n    result_rationale: >\n      随着 attention ratio 增加，aggregate convergence 增强（std 从 0.024 降到 0.005）\n      而 per-example divergence 也增强（Jaccard 从 0.08 降到 0.04，意味着 helped/hurt\n      subsets 越来越不重叠）。两者负相关（r=-0.94）是 paradox 的数学必然：当各架构\n      的 aggregate 趋同但 per-example effect magnitude 增大时，唯一的解释是各架构在\n      不同 sample 上做了更大幅度的\"互补性\"调整。更多 attention = 更强的补偿效应 =\n      aggregate 更趋同 + per-example 更 divergent。Net effect asymmetry（GDN 和 RetNet\n      net negative, HGRN2 net positive）在所有 attention ratio 保持方向一致但幅度\n      随 ratio 增大，呈现对称但相反的效应——这就是 \"equalizer paradox\" 的核心可视化。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Convergence-divergence co-evolution by attention ratio\"\n        columns: [\"Attention ratio\", \"Cross-arch std\", \"Jaccard (mean pairwise)\", \"GDN net effect\", \"RetNet net effect\", \"HGRN2 net effect\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0 (pure recurrent)\", \"0.024\", \"—\", \"0.00\", \"0.00\", \"0.00\"]\n          - [\"1\", \"0.018\", \"0.08\", \"-0.03\", \"-0.02\", \"+0.03\"]\n          - [\"3\", \"0.012\", \"0.07\", \"-0.06\", \"-0.04\", \"+0.06\"]\n          - [\"6\", \"0.008\", \"0.06\", \"-0.09\", \"-0.06\", \"+0.08\"]\n          - [\"8\", \"0.007\", \"0.05\", \"-0.10\", \"-0.07\", \"+0.10\"]\n          - [\"24\", \"0.005\", \"0.04\", \"-0.12\", \"-0.08\", \"+0.11\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 9a (论文 hero figure): Dual y-axis plot，x=attention ratio。Left y=cross-arch std（下降曲线，蓝色）。Right y=Jaccard mean（下降曲线，红色）。两条曲线同向下降，标注 r=-0.94。Title: 'The Equalizer Paradox'。\"\n      - \"Fig 9b: Stacked bar chart，x=attention ratio，y=net effect per architecture。GDN 和 RetNet 向下（负），HGRN2 向上（正）。各 bar 的绝对值随 ratio 增大，但正负对称，aggregate 趋向零。\"\n      - \"Fig 9c: 示意图——三个架构的 helped/hurt Venn diagram 在 ratio=1 和 ratio=24 时的对比，显示 overlap 随 attention 增加而减少。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Convergence-divergence co-evolution（r=-0.94, p=0.005）是 paper 的 hero result，\n      直接可视化了 title 中的 \"Equalizer Paradox\"。这不是一个偶然发现，而是 attention\n      作为\"equalizer\"的内在机制：它通过在不同架构上做不同的事来实现 aggregate 趋同。\n      Net effect asymmetry 的对称性（GDN/RetNet hurt, HGRN2 helped, 幅度近似）表明\n      convergence 不是某个架构\"被拉上来\"，而是所有架构\"被推向中间\"——这与 paper title\n      \"Equalizer\" 的隐喻完美对应。此图应作为 paper 的 Figure 1 或 graphical abstract。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10641,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10641},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc1945c5-caea-4246-8ef4-0ee4426cff4c","uuid":"8e8ba54a-b502-4e0b-882b-3ebd30376a9a"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":210545,"duration_api_ms":211790,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  所有实验均确认或加强现有发现。Continuous retrieval-demand spectrum 成立且有 ≥2 个锚点\n  （LAMBADA ρ=-1.0, ARC-Easy ρ≈-0.85）。Mechanistic evidence 完整：sample feature\n  区分 + attention pattern 相关性形成因果链。额外架构（Mamba hybrid）复现收敛模式。\n  340M rebound 有 capacity bottleneck 解释，与 1.3B 形成连贯叙事。GDN 排除后三条 claim\n  均成立。直投 EMNLP Main，title 用 \"The Equalizer Paradox\"。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Task-specificity characterization of equalizer effect\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      对 6 个 benchmark 计算 1.3B 下各 attention ratio 的 cross-architecture std，\n      建立 convergence strength（Spearman ρ）与 retrieval demand 的连续关系。\n    expected_results:\n      lambada_rho: -1.0\n      lambada_std_reduction_pct: 79\n      arc_easy_rho: -0.7\n      arc_challenge_rho: -0.3\n      hellaswag_rho: -0.1\n      winogrande_rho: 0.05\n      mmlu_rho: 0.1\n      benchmarks_with_rho_below_neg05: 2\n    result_rationale: >\n      LAMBADA 是纯 last-word retrieval 任务，attention 的 key-value lookup 机制天然对齐\n      这类需求，因此跨架构方差压缩最彻底（ρ=-1.0）。ARC-Easy 含大量事实检索型题目，\n      attention 部分有效（ρ=-0.7）。HellaSwag/WinoGrande/MMLU 以推理、常识、世界知识为主，\n      attention 的收敛作用被 recurrence core 的架构差异主导，ρ 趋近零。这形成了以 retrieval\n      demand 为横轴的 dose-response 曲线，两个显著锚点（LAMBADA + ARC-Easy）足以建立\n      continuous spectrum 的可信度。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Cross-architecture convergence by benchmark\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Retrieval Demand (BIG-bench)\", \"ρ (std vs attn ratio)\", \"p-value (permutation)\", \"Std at ratio=0\", \"Std at ratio=24\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LAMBADA\", \"High\", \"-1.00\", \"0.0083\", \"0.024\", \"0.005\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Easy\", \"Medium-High\", \"-0.70\", \"0.117\", \"0.031\", \"0.018\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Challenge\", \"Medium\", \"-0.30\", \"0.347\", \"0.022\", \"0.019\"]\n          - [\"HellaSwag\", \"Low\", \"-0.10\", \"0.782\", \"0.018\", \"0.017\"]\n          - [\"WinoGrande\", \"Low-Medium\", \"0.05\", \"0.912\", \"0.015\", \"0.016\"]\n          - [\"MMLU\", \"Low\", \"0.10\", \"0.782\", \"0.028\", \"0.027\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 1a: 散点图，x=retrieval demand（连续量化），y=Spearman ρ，6 个 benchmark 标注。拟合线 R²≈0.85，显示 dose-response 关系。\"\n      - \"Fig 1b: 折线图，x=attention ratio (0,1,3,6,8,24)，y=cross-arch std，每条线一个 benchmark。LAMBADA 单调下降，ARC-Easy 下降但较平缓，其余平坦。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Continuous retrieval-demand spectrum 成立。避免了 binary retrieval/reasoning 分类的\n      post-hoc cherry-picking 风险。BIG-bench taxonomy 提供外部锚定。LAMBADA + ARC-Easy\n      两个锚点形成梯度，其余 benchmark 填充低端。Reviewer Concern B 通过 dose-response\n      framing 化解。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark per-example analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      对 1.3B 模型（GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 × 5 attention ratios）和 10×340M 模型重新运行\n      lm-eval --log_samples，收集 HellaSwag、ARC-Easy、ARC-Challenge 的 per-example 数据。\n      分析 per-example 层面是否存在 convergence 或 task-specific divergence。\n    expected_results:\n      hellaswag_per_example_convergence: false\n      hellaswag_per_example_pattern: \"systematic architecture-specific, not random noise\"\n      arc_easy_per_example_convergence: true\n      arc_easy_rho_after_per_example: -0.85\n      arc_easy_jaccard_pairwise: 0.12\n      arc_challenge_per_example_convergence: false\n      arc_challenge_per_example_pattern: \"weak, architecture-independent noise\"\n      models_evaluated: 23\n      gpu_hours_actual: 18\n    result_rationale: >\n      HellaSwag 在 aggregate 层面无收敛（ρ=-0.1），per-example 分析确认这不是 power 问题而是\n      真阴性——attention 在不同架构上改变不同 sample 的正确率，但这些变化是 systematic\n      architecture-specific（每个架构有自己稳定的 helped/hurt subset），而非 random noise。\n      这说明 attention 在推理任务上\"做了事\"但没有跨架构趋同。ARC-Easy 在 per-example 层面\n      发现 attention 确实压缩了跨架构差异：对 retrieval-heavy 子题（事实召回型），三个架构的\n      正确率 variance 下降；对 reasoning-heavy 子题则无变化。这将 aggregate ρ 从 -0.70\n      加强至 -0.85（通过去除 reasoning 子题噪声）。ARC-Easy 成为 continuous spectrum 的\n      第二个强锚点。ARC-Challenge 因推理占比高，per-example 无系统模式。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Per-example convergence metrics by benchmark\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"N samples\", \"Aggregate ρ\", \"Per-example ρ (filtered)\", \"Jaccard (pairwise mean)\", \"Pattern type\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LAMBADA\", \"5153\", \"-1.00\", \"-1.00\", \"0.06\", \"Architecture-specific convergence\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Easy\", \"2376\", \"-0.70\", \"-0.85\", \"0.12\", \"Retrieval-subset convergence\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Challenge\", \"1172\", \"-0.30\", \"-0.25\", \"0.31\", \"No systematic pattern\"]\n          - [\"HellaSwag\", \"10042\", \"-0.10\", \"-0.08\", \"0.22\", \"Systematic but non-converging\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 2a: Heatmap，rows=HellaSwag samples (clustered)，cols=models (sorted by arch×attn ratio)。显示 per-example correctness pattern 是 architecture-clustered 而非 attention-ratio-clustered，确认非收敛。\"\n      - \"Fig 2b: ARC-Easy 子集分析——retrieval-type vs reasoning-type 题目分别画 cross-arch std 曲线。Retrieval 子集下降明显（ρ=-0.85），reasoning 子集平坦。\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-002 的 best 结果是双重确认：(1) HellaSwag/ARC-C 在 per-example 层面确认非收敛，\n      升级 task-specificity 从\"aggregate insignificant\"到\"per-example confirmed non-converging\"；\n      (2) ARC-Easy 在去噪后 ρ 加强至 -0.85，成为第二个强锚点。Continuous spectrum 从\n      单点（LAMBADA）变为双锚点梯度，极大加强 Claim 1。\n\n  - name: \"Helped/hurt sample characterization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对 LAMBADA 上各架构的 helped/hurt samples 计算 token frequency、context length、\n      last-sentence perplexity、domain 分布。测试 feature 是否区分 helped/hurt，且跨架构\n      feature profile 是否不同。\n    expected_results:\n      n_features_significant_p001: 3\n      best_feature: \"target_token_frequency\"\n      best_feature_p: 2.5e-05\n      second_feature: \"context_length\"\n      second_feature_p: 3.1e-04\n      third_feature: \"last_sentence_perplexity\"\n      third_feature_p: 8.7e-04\n      gdn_profile: \"helped on rare tokens + long contexts\"\n      retnet_profile: \"helped on high-perplexity last sentences\"\n      hgrn2_profile: \"helped broadly but strongest on medium-frequency tokens\"\n      cross_arch_profile_difference_p: 0.0003\n      effect_size_cohens_d_best: 0.72\n    result_rationale: >\n      GatedDeltaNet 的 delta rule 机制擅长 associative recall，attention 补充的是对\n      rare token 的 precise retrieval（delta rule 对 rare token 的 update 不够精确），\n      因此 GDN helped samples 集中在 rare token + long context（需要远距离检索）。RetNet\n      的 exponential decay 使其对 last sentence 内的局部信息较强，attention 补充的是\n      high-perplexity last sentence 中的 disambiguation（decay 无法区分多个候选），因此\n      RetNet helped samples 集中在 high-perplexity last sentence。HGRN2 的 hierarchical\n      gating 提供多尺度记忆但对 token frequency 有 sweet spot，attention 拓宽了这个\n      sweet spot。三种架构的 feature profile 统计显著不同（p<0.001），这直接解释了为什么\n      Jaccard overlap 低——它们被 attention 帮助的 sample 具有不同的语言学特征。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Feature importance for helped/hurt classification by architecture\"\n        columns: [\"Feature\", \"GDN (AUC)\", \"RetNet (AUC)\", \"HGRN2 (AUC)\", \"Overall p-value\", \"Cross-arch difference p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Target token freq (log rank)\", \"0.71\", \"0.58\", \"0.64\", \"2.5e-05\", \"0.0012\"]\n          - [\"Context length (tokens)\", \"0.67\", \"0.55\", \"0.57\", \"3.1e-04\", \"0.0089\"]\n          - [\"Last-sentence perplexity\", \"0.56\", \"0.69\", \"0.61\", \"8.7e-04\", \"0.0003\"]\n          - [\"Domain (topic entropy)\", \"0.54\", \"0.53\", \"0.55\", \"0.042\", \"0.31\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 3a: 三列 violin plot，每列一个架构，y=target token frequency，分 helped/hurt。GDN 的 helped 明显偏 rare（高 rank），RetNet 和 HGRN2 差异较小。\"\n      - \"Fig 3b: Radar chart，三个架构各一条线，四个 feature 为轴。显示 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 各有不同的 feature profile 'shape'，视觉化 mechanism specificity。\"\n      - \"Fig 3c: 2D embedding (UMAP on feature space)，helped samples 用架构颜色标注。三个架构的 helped clusters 空间分离。\"\n    analysis: >\n      3 个 feature 在 p<0.001 水平显著区分 helped/hurt，且跨架构 profile 统计显著不同。\n      这为 Claim 3（architecture-specific mechanism）提供了 feature-level 解释：不是抽象的\n      \"不同 sample\"，而是\"不同语言学特征的 sample\"。Feature profile 差异直接映射到各架构\n      recurrence core 的已知机制特性（delta rule → rare token recall; exponential decay\n      → local disambiguation; hierarchical gating → multi-scale memory）。\n\n  - name: \"Attention weight extraction and visualization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      从 h3-1 配置的三个架构提取 attention weight，分析 attention pattern 与 per-example\n      helped/hurt identity 的相关性，以及跨架构 attention pattern 的相似度。\n    expected_results:\n      attention_per_example_correlation_gdn: 0.52\n      attention_per_example_correlation_retnet: 0.61\n      attention_per_example_correlation_hgrn2: 0.48\n      attention_per_example_correlation_mean: 0.54\n      cross_arch_attention_similarity: 0.23\n      gdn_attention_focus: \"distributed over long-range context tokens\"\n      retnet_attention_focus: \"concentrated on last-sentence tokens\"\n      hgrn2_attention_focus: \"hierarchical — split between local and mid-range\"\n      gpu_hours_actual: 3.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      Attention layer 在不同 recurrence backbone 上学到了不同的 attention pattern，因为\n      它在补偿各架构 recurrence core 的不同弱点。GDN 的 delta rule 已经做了一定的\n      associative memory，attention 学会关注 long-range context（补充 delta rule 的\n      远距离衰减）。RetNet 的 exponential decay 快速遗忘远距离信息，attention 集中在\n      last-sentence 内做 disambiguation（因为 RetNet 对近距离信息已经较强）。HGRN2 的\n      hierarchical gating 在多个尺度上保留信息但每个尺度都不够精确，attention 学会\n      hierarchical 分配。这些不同的 attention pattern 与 helped/hurt sample 的对应关系\n      ≥0.4（最高 RetNet 0.61），因为 attention 的\"关注什么\"直接决定了\"帮助哪些 sample\"。\n      跨架构 attention similarity 仅 0.23，远低于随机基线 0.5，这是 mechanistic evidence\n      的核心：同样的 attention 架构在不同 recurrence backbone 上学到了完全不同的行为。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Attention pattern analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Attention focus\", \"Corr with helped/hurt\", \"p-value\", \"Mean entropy\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GDN\", \"Long-range distributed\", \"0.52\", \"1.2e-04\", \"3.41\"]\n          - [\"RetNet\", \"Last-sentence concentrated\", \"0.61\", \"8.7e-06\", \"2.18\"]\n          - [\"HGRN2\", \"Hierarchical split\", \"0.48\", \"4.3e-04\", \"2.89\"]\n      - name: \"Table 4b: Cross-architecture attention similarity (cosine)\"\n        columns: [\"Pair\", \"Mean cosine sim\", \"Significance vs random baseline\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GDN-RetNet\", \"0.19\", \"p<0.001 (below random)\"]\n          - [\"GDN-HGRN2\", \"0.27\", \"p=0.003 (below random)\"]\n          - [\"RetNet-HGRN2\", \"0.24\", \"p=0.001 (below random)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 4a: 三个 attention heatmap（每架构一个），同一组 LAMBADA sample，sorted by helped/hurt。可视化 attention 在 helped sample 上的 pattern 差异。\"\n      - \"Fig 4b: Attention entropy distribution per architecture。RetNet 的 attention 最集中（低 entropy），GDN 最分散。\"\n      - \"Fig 4c: 因果链图示：recurrence mechanism → attention adaptation → sample-specific effect → aggregate convergence。用箭头和数值标注每步的 correlation。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Mean correlation 0.54（range 0.48–0.61）超过 pass_fail 阈值 0.4，提供了 mechanistic\n      evidence 的第二根支柱。与 exp-003 的 feature 分析合在一起，形成完整因果链：\n      recurrence core 特性 → attention 学到补偿性 pattern → 补偿作用在不同语言学特征\n      的 sample 上生效 → 各架构 aggregate 性能趋同但 per-example 效果不重叠。\n      这回应 Reviewer Concern C（\"no causal mechanism\"），从 correlation 升级到\n      directed mechanistic narrative。\n\n  - name: \"Architecture expansion check\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      搜索 Wang et al. model zoo 及其他来源，找到额外的 hybrid 架构（Mamba hybrid 等），\n      在 LAMBADA 上评估收敛模式是否复现。\n    expected_results:\n      additional_architectures_found: 1\n      architecture_name: \"Mamba2-Attn hybrid (from community reproduction)\"\n      architecture_type: \"selective state space + attention\"\n      lambada_convergence_confirmed: true\n      mamba2_rho: -0.90\n      mamba2_std_reduction_pct: 71\n      mamba2_jaccard_with_others: 0.05\n      total_architectures_tested: 4\n      gpu_hours_actual: 5\n    result_rationale: >\n      Mamba2 的 selective state space mechanism 与 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 的 linear recurrence\n      不同（selection mechanism vs gating/delta rule/exponential decay），但 attention\n      的补偿效应仍然成立：Mamba2 的 state selection 对某类 retrieval pattern 较弱，\n      attention 补充后 aggregate 性能趋同。ρ=-0.90（略弱于 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 的 -1.0）\n      可能因为 Mamba2 hybrid 的 attention 集成方式略有不同（interleaved vs stacked），\n      但趋势一致。Jaccard 0.05 表明 Mamba2 的 helped/hurt subset 与其他三个架构同样\n      不重叠，进一步支持 architecture-specific mechanism。n=4 架构使得 Reviewer Concern D\n      （\"n=3 too few\"）大幅缓解。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Architecture expansion — convergence on LAMBADA\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Recurrence type\", \"ρ (std vs attn ratio)\", \"Std reduction %\", \"Jaccard with GDN\", \"Jaccard with RetNet\", \"Jaccard with HGRN2\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GDN\", \"Gated delta rule\", \"-1.00\", \"79%\", \"—\", \"0.06\", \"0.04\"]\n          - [\"RetNet\", \"Linear attn + exp decay\", \"-1.00\", \"79%\", \"0.06\", \"—\", \"0.08\"]\n          - [\"HGRN2\", \"Hierarchical gating\", \"-1.00\", \"79%\", \"0.04\", \"0.08\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Mamba2-Attn\", \"Selective state space\", \"-0.90\", \"71%\", \"0.05\", \"0.04\", \"0.07\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 5: 四条 convergence 曲线（cross-arch std vs attention ratio），LAMBADA。原三架构 + Mamba2-Attn。Mamba2 曲线形状一致但略高，汇入同一趋势。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Mamba2-Attn 的加入将 architectures_tested 从 3 提升到 4，覆盖了四种不同的 recurrence\n      mechanism。收敛模式复现（ρ=-0.90, std reduction 71%），且 Jaccard 保持低水平，\n      说明 equalizer effect 不是三个特定架构的巧合，而是 attention + any recurrence 的\n      通用现象。这是 generalization evidence 的最佳结果，直接提升论文的 impact 和\n      reviewer 的信任度。\n\n  - name: \"340M rebound mechanism analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      深入分析 340M 在 attn=8 时的非单调 rebound。与 1.3B 同 attention ratio 做\n      per-example 对比，识别 diverge 的 sample 并 characterize rebound 机制。\n    expected_results:\n      rebound_mechanism: \"capacity bottleneck\"\n      rebound_explanation: >\n        340M 在 attn ratio=8 时，attention 参数占总参数比例过高（~30%），\n        压缩了 recurrence core 的有效容量。Recurrence core 性能下降的 sample\n        与 attention 新帮助的 sample 不完全重叠，导致 aggregate std 回升。\n      rebound_samples_n: 412\n      rebound_samples_overlap_with_1_3b_hurt: 0.73\n      capacity_ratio_at_rebound: 0.31\n      capacity_ratio_at_monotonic_1_3b: 0.12\n      scale_contrast_narrative: >\n        1.3B 有足够容量同时支持 recurrence core 和 attention，两者互补；\n        340M 在高 attention ratio 时两者竞争参数预算，形成 capacity bottleneck。\n      training_tokens_confound_ruled_out: true\n      confound_evidence: \"per-example rebound pattern matches capacity prediction, not token-count prediction\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      340M 模型总参数有限，attention layer 的参数开销在 ratio=8 时占比达到 ~31%，\n      远高于 1.3B 同 ratio 时的 ~12%。这种参数预算竞争导致 recurrence core 的\n      effective capacity 下降。具体表现为：340M 在 ratio=8 时有 412 个 sample\n      从 correct 变为 incorrect（这些 sample 在 ratio=6 时还是 correct），其中 73%\n      在 1.3B ratio=8 时仍然 correct——说明问题在于 capacity 而非 attention 本身的\n      负面效应。训练 token 数量差异（20B vs 100B）作为 confound 被排除：如果是 token\n      count 导致，则 rebound 应该在所有 sample 上均匀分布；但实际 rebound 集中在\n      需要 strong recurrence（长距离依赖 + 高 token frequency）的 sample 上，\n      符合 capacity bottleneck 预测而非 token-count 预测。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: 340M rebound characterization\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"340M ratio=6\", \"340M ratio=8 (rebound)\", \"1.3B ratio=8\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Cross-arch std\", \"0.009\", \"0.014\", \"0.006\", \"340M rebounds, 1.3B continues declining\"]\n          - [\"Attention param ratio\", \"0.23\", \"0.31\", \"0.12\", \"340M capacity squeeze at ratio=8\"]\n          - [\"Rebound samples (became incorrect)\", \"—\", \"412\", \"0 (still correct)\", \"Capacity bottleneck\"]\n          - [\"Rebound sample features\", \"—\", \"Long context + high-freq tokens\", \"N/A\", \"Needs strong recurrence\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 6a: Dual y-axis plot，x=attention ratio。Left y=cross-arch std（340M 和 1.3B 两条线）。Right y=attention param ratio。340M 在 param ratio>0.3 处 rebound，1.3B 在 param ratio<0.15 范围内持续下降。\"\n      - \"Fig 6b: Venn diagram，340M rebound samples vs 1.3B hurt samples。73% overlap 标注。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Capacity bottleneck 机制清晰且有 falsifiable prediction（如果是 capacity 问题，\n      则 rebound samples 应集中在 recurrence-demanding 特征上——已验证）。排除了\n      training token confound。340M vs 1.3B 的对比从 aggregate 观察（\"scale matters\"）\n      升级为 mechanistic explanation（\"sufficient capacity is prerequisite for attention\n      to complement rather than compete with recurrence\"）。这为 Claim 2 提供了\n      two-scale 情况下能达到的最强叙事。\n\n  - name: \"Statistical robustness framework\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      Bootstrap CI、多重比较校正、GDN 排除敏感性分析、effect size 报告。\n    expected_results:\n      lambada_std_reduction_bootstrap_ci_pct: [72, 86]\n      lambada_std_reduction_point: 79\n      lambada_rho_bootstrap_ci: [-1.0, -0.90]\n      lambada_rho_point: -1.0\n      bonferroni_corrected_lambada_p: 0.050\n      fdr_corrected_lambada_p: 0.025\n      lambada_survives_correction: true\n      arc_easy_survives_correction: false\n      gdn_excluded_lambada_rho: -1.0\n      gdn_excluded_std_reduction: 74\n      gdn_excluded_claim1_survives: true\n      gdn_excluded_claim2_survives: true\n      gdn_excluded_claim3_survives: true\n      claims_surviving_gdn_exclusion: 3\n      cohens_d_lambada_convergence: 1.84\n      eta_squared_attention_ratio_effect: 0.67\n      bootstrap_iterations: 10000\n    result_rationale: >\n      LAMBADA 的 convergence effect size 极大（Cohen's d=1.84），Bootstrap 10000 次\n      迭代后 CI [72%, 86%] 不跨零，即使取下界 72% 仍是强效应。Bonferroni 校正\n      （6 benchmarks → α=0.0083）后 LAMBADA 仍显著（原始 p=0.0083，校正后刚好\n      在边界但通过），FDR 校正更宽松（p=0.025）。ARC-Easy 因 power 不足在 Bonferroni\n      后不显著（p=0.117），但在 continuous spectrum 叙事中作为\"suggestive\"仍有价值。\n      GDN 排除后（n=2 架构 + Mamba2），LAMBADA ρ 保持 -1.0（RetNet 和 HGRN2 本身就\n      呈现完美单调收敛），std reduction 从 79% 降至 74%（因样本量减少，估计略保守），\n      但三条 claim 均成立。这是因为 GDN 虽有 D004 confound，但 convergence 不依赖 GDN——\n      任意两个架构之间都呈现收敛。Claim 3 在 GDN 排除后也成立因为 RetNet vs HGRN2 的\n      Jaccard 仅 0.08，且 effect direction 相反（RetNet hurt, HGRN2 helped）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Bootstrap confidence intervals\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Point estimate\", \"Bootstrap 95% CI\", \"Survives Bonferroni?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LAMBADA std reduction %\", \"79%\", \"[72%, 86%]\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"LAMBADA ρ\", \"-1.00\", \"[-1.00, -0.90]\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Easy ρ\", \"-0.85\", \"[-1.00, -0.50]\", \"No (suggestive)\"]\n          - [\"Cross-arch Jaccard mean\", \"0.06\", \"[0.03, 0.09]\", \"N/A\"]\n      - name: \"Table 7b: GDN exclusion sensitivity\"\n        columns: [\"Claim\", \"With GDN\", \"Without GDN\", \"Survives?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Claim 1 (task-specific convergence)\", \"ρ=-1.0, 79% reduction\", \"ρ=-1.0, 74% reduction\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"Claim 2 (scale-dependent)\", \"340M partial, 1.3B complete\", \"Same pattern (RetNet/HGRN2/Mamba2)\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"Claim 3 (arch-specific mechanism)\", \"Jaccard=0.06, 3 profiles\", \"Jaccard=0.08, 2+1 profiles\", \"Yes\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 7: Bootstrap distribution plots。Left: std reduction %（vertical line at 0，distribution 远在右侧）。Right: ρ（distribution 远在 -1 附近）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      统计框架完整且所有核心 claim 通过 robustness check。GDN exclusion 是最关键的\n      sensitivity test（因为 GDN 有 D004 confound），三条 claim 均成立。LAMBADA 在\n      多重比较后仍显著是 best tier 的关键指标——Bonferroni 边界通过（p=0.0083 for\n      6 tests, observed p=0.0083）。Bootstrap CI 范围 [72%, 86%] 完全落在 best tier\n      指标范围 [70, 88] 内。\n\n  - name: \"Wang et al. explicit differentiation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      逐点对比 Wang et al. 的 exact statements 与我们的分析，建立清晰的四点增量。\n    expected_results:\n      wang_convergence_mentions: 3\n      wang_quantitative_convergence: 0\n      wang_per_example_analysis: 0\n      wang_scale_dependent_analysis: 0\n      wang_mechanistic_analysis: 0\n      differentiation_points: 4\n      wang_exact_quotes_extracted: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      Wang et al. 的论文是 model zoo paper，核心贡献是训练并开源 72 个模型。他们对\n      convergence 的提及限于 qualitative observations（如 \"performance gap narrows\n      with more attention layers\"），没有 (a) 计算 cross-arch std trajectories 或\n      Spearman ρ，(b) 做 per-example analysis，(c) 分析 scale dependency of convergence，\n      (d) 提供 mechanistic explanation。我们的增量恰好是他们没做的四件事。这四点\n      differentiation 在 paper 中以 explicit side-by-side table 呈现，让 reviewer\n      一目了然。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Systematic comparison with Wang et al. (2025)\"\n        columns: [\"Analysis dimension\", \"Wang et al.\", \"This work\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Cross-arch convergence quantification\", \"Qualitative ('gap narrows')\", \"Spearman ρ=-1.0, std reduction 79%, bootstrap CI\"]\n          - [\"Per-example mechanism\", \"Not analyzed\", \"Jaccard<0.10, architecture-specific helped/hurt subsets\"]\n          - [\"Scale dependency\", \"Not analyzed\", \"Binary contrast: 340M partial (rebound) vs 1.3B complete, capacity bottleneck mechanism\"]\n          - [\"Task-specificity\", \"Not analyzed\", \"Continuous retrieval-demand spectrum, 6 benchmarks, dose-response curve\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 8: Side-by-side visualization。Left: Wang et al. 的 aggregate performance table（screenshot with citation）。Right: 我们的 convergence curve + per-example heatmap，annotated with the four increments。\"\n    analysis: >\n      四点 differentiation 清晰且无重叠。我们使用 Wang et al. 的 model zoo（proper\n      attribution）但提供了他们完全没有的分析维度。这回应 Reviewer Risk 4 和 Concern E，\n      将我们的贡献从\"also studied convergence\"提升到\"discovered and characterized a\n      phenomenon they only glimpsed qualitatively\"。\n\n  - name: \"Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      在 LAMBADA 上，以 attention ratio 为 x 轴，同时绘制 aggregate convergence（cross-arch std）\n      和 per-example divergence（Jaccard, net effect asymmetry），展示 paradox 的共同演化。\n    expected_results:\n      convergence_divergence_correlation: -0.94\n      convergence_divergence_p: 0.005\n      paradox_strengthens_with_attention: true\n      jaccard_at_ratio_0: \"N/A (no attention effect)\"\n      jaccard_at_ratio_1: 0.08\n      jaccard_at_ratio_6: 0.06\n      jaccard_at_ratio_24: 0.04\n      std_at_ratio_0: 0.024\n      std_at_ratio_24: 0.005\n      net_effect_asymmetry_gdn: -0.12\n      net_effect_asymmetry_retnet: -0.08\n      net_effect_asymmetry_hgrn2: 0.11\n    result_rationale: >\n      随着 attention ratio 增加，aggregate convergence 增强（std 从 0.024 降到 0.005）\n      而 per-example divergence 也增强（Jaccard 从 0.08 降到 0.04，意味着 helped/hurt\n      subsets 越来越不重叠）。两者负相关（r=-0.94）是 paradox 的数学必然：当各架构\n      的 aggregate 趋同但 per-example effect magnitude 增大时，唯一的解释是各架构在\n      不同 sample 上做了更大幅度的\"互补性\"调整。更多 attention = 更强的补偿效应 =\n      aggregate 更趋同 + per-example 更 divergent。Net effect asymmetry（GDN 和 RetNet\n      net negative, HGRN2 net positive）在所有 attention ratio 保持方向一致但幅度\n      随 ratio 增大，呈现对称但相反的效应——这就是 \"equalizer paradox\" 的核心可视化。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Convergence-divergence co-evolution by attention ratio\"\n        columns: [\"Attention ratio\", \"Cross-arch std\", \"Jaccard (mean pairwise)\", \"GDN net effect\", \"RetNet net effect\", \"HGRN2 net effect\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0 (pure recurrent)\", \"0.024\", \"—\", \"0.00\", \"0.00\", \"0.00\"]\n          - [\"1\", \"0.018\", \"0.08\", \"-0.03\", \"-0.02\", \"+0.03\"]\n          - [\"3\", \"0.012\", \"0.07\", \"-0.06\", \"-0.04\", \"+0.06\"]\n          - [\"6\", \"0.008\", \"0.06\", \"-0.09\", \"-0.06\", \"+0.08\"]\n          - [\"8\", \"0.007\", \"0.05\", \"-0.10\", \"-0.07\", \"+0.10\"]\n          - [\"24\", \"0.005\", \"0.04\", \"-0.12\", \"-0.08\", \"+0.11\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 9a (论文 hero figure): Dual y-axis plot，x=attention ratio。Left y=cross-arch std（下降曲线，蓝色）。Right y=Jaccard mean（下降曲线，红色）。两条曲线同向下降，标注 r=-0.94。Title: 'The Equalizer Paradox'。\"\n      - \"Fig 9b: Stacked bar chart，x=attention ratio，y=net effect per architecture。GDN 和 RetNet 向下（负），HGRN2 向上（正）。各 bar 的绝对值随 ratio 增大，但正负对称，aggregate 趋向零。\"\n      - \"Fig 9c: 示意图——三个架构的 helped/hurt Venn diagram 在 ratio=1 和 ratio=24 时的对比，显示 overlap 随 attention 增加而减少。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Convergence-divergence co-evolution（r=-0.94, p=0.005）是 paper 的 hero result，\n      直接可视化了 title 中的 \"Equalizer Paradox\"。这不是一个偶然发现，而是 attention\n      作为\"equalizer\"的内在机制：它通过在不同架构上做不同的事来实现 aggregate 趋同。\n      Net effect asymmetry 的对称性（GDN/RetNet hurt, HGRN2 helped, 幅度近似）表明\n      convergence 不是某个架构\"被拉上来\"，而是所有架构\"被推向中间\"——这与 paper title\n      \"Equalizer\" 的隐喻完美对应。此图应作为 paper 的 Figure 1 或 graphical abstract。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"cc1945c5-caea-4246-8ef4-0ee4426cff4c","total_cost_usd":0.35041675,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10641,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":10891,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10641,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":10891,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10641,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10641},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":5600,"outputTokens":21,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"cos